275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (          lmost exactly one year ago, I proposed to do a research paper using Stacker News data \(#1243188\) and to do so in public, with all the code available in a public github repo, and regular public updates on the progress of the research.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (The first set of results were finished in around December 2025, and since then I've been trying to get it accepted at conferences and journals.  Unfortunately, the track record was not great.  A Bitcoin research conference did not take it \(no reason given\), the Journal of Economic Behavior and Organization did not take it \(too niche\), and Electronics Commerce Research and Applications did not take it \(I don't write like an IS scholar\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (But, I'm pleased to say that finally we are having some success. The paper was just accepted to the Workshop on Information Systems and Economics, which will be held in Lisbon, Portugal this December.  This is one of the main conferences for economists studying information systems, and the program looks super interesting.  I think this is the right group of people to try and get this work in front of, and I'm looking forward to the feedback I get -- as well as the exposure Stacker News may receive from other researchers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
